  "description": "JULWEU crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C124 H210 Cu4 Gd8 N6 O52,3.4(C2 H3 N1),0.4(C1 H4 O1),0.7(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Cu1 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1A (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu2A (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd4A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.286-4.587 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 81.88-138.01°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Cu4Gd8(OH)6(NO3)2(O2CCH2But)16(pdm)4]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
